  "desc": "A 1.42B-parameter model: 52 unique layers at width 1536, with a 20-layer block in the middle run twice for 72 effective layers, and attention-residual boundaries fitted to the network's own layer geometry. The trunk trains at a constant learning rate to 100B tokens; annealed reads are cooldown branches forked from its checkpoints (cosine decay to zero over about 10% of the tokens so far). The release is the 110B branch from the 100B fork. A second anneal from the same fork, with identical training loss, reads .025 bits/byte worse on held-out text: single-anneal numbers carry that spread. A second initialization seed (seed 7, same data order) was trained to 11B."
